d1-2B Decide Android sample

Model: d1-2B by Liquid AI, Inc. (huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-2B, revision
10e7671d44e4b37700020b1eed3f594c5f2af0b4), licensed under the LFM Open License v1.0 (LICENSE,
unchanged). The LiteRT graphs, the embedding table and the provider files the app loads come from
the model repository litert-community/d1-2B-LiteRT, a converted and modified Derivative Work of that
model whose NOTICE lists the changes. They are copied to the phone, not kept in this source tree.

The host is a Kotlin port of the Python code that ships with the model (same revision, LFM Open
License v1.0), so the app builds the same prompts and reads the same answers as the model's own
code; each ported file carries a notice that it was ported and changed:
- Prompt.kt: prompt.py, grid.py and parts of attention.py
- Answers.kt: api.py, box.py, calibration.py, json_spans.py and parts of pointer.py
- Parsing.kt: parsing.py
- Host.kt: the sequence packing of attention.py, the slot reading of runner.py, the pointer reads
  of pointer.py and the readouts of prompt.py
- Pictures.kt: smart_resize of the model's image processor (image_processing_lfm3_vl.py)
Changes: Kotlin instead of Python; one request per call with at most one picture; the language
model and the picture tower run as LiteRT graphs on the GPU at FP32 (the conversion in
litert-community/d1-2B-LiteRT), with the embedding rows looked up on the host and the output rows
read only for each question's options.

Tokenizer.kt implements byte-level BPE as the Hugging Face tokenizers library does (Apache License
2.0, licenses/Tokenizers-APACHE-2.0.txt): https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers

Pictures.kt ports PyTorch's antialiased bicubic resize of uint8 images
(aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/UpSampleKernel.cpp), BSD-3-Clause (licenses/PyTorch-BSD-3-Clause.txt):
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch

app/src/main/assets/bike.png: "Bike on a snowy street in Quebec City at night" by Wilfredor,
CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication), Wikimedia Commons:
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bike_on_a_snowy_street_in_Quebec_City_at_night.jpg
Resized to 384 x 256 pixels.

The texts, the JSON record and the questions of app/src/main/assets/examples.json were written for
this sample; their people, businesses, addresses and numbers are invented.
